\details{
This function converts the mean difference (MD) 95\% CI into a standard error,
and then relies on the calculations of the \code{\link{es_from_ancova_md_se}} function.

\strong{To convert the 95\% CI into a standard error,} the following formula is used (table 12.3 in Cooper):
\deqn{md\_se = \frac{ancova\_md\_ci\_up - ancova\_md\_ci\_lo}{(2 * qt(0.975, n\_exp + n\_nexp - 2 - n\_cov\_ancova))}}
Calculations of the \code{\link{es_from_ancova_md_se}()} are then applied.
}
\note{
This route has to assume the two groups were balanced on the covariate; when they were
not, the effect size and its standard error are both attenuated. Prefer
\code{\link{es_from_ancova_md_sd}()} when the residual standard deviation is
reported.
